{
  "id": "PHP.3",
  "number": "3",
  "bookId": "PHP",
  "reference": "Philippians 3",
  "verseCount": 21,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "3",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "PHP 3"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "3",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, my brethren, rejoice in the Lord. To write the same things to you, to me indeed is not irksome, but for you it is safe. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Beware of the dogs, beware of the evil workers, beware of the concision: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "for we are the circumcision, who worship by the Spirit of God, and glory in Christ Jesus, and have no confidence in the flesh: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "though I myself might have confidence even in the flesh: if any other man thinketh to have confidence in the flesh, I yet more: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "circumcised the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews; as touching the law, a Pharisee; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "as touching zeal, persecuting the church; as touching the righteousness which is in the law, found blameless. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Howbeit what things were gain to me, these have I counted loss for Christ. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Yea verily, and I count all things to be loss for the excellency of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord: for whom I suffered the loss of all things, and do count them but refuse, that I may gain Christ, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and be found in him, not having a righteousness of mine own, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " that which is of the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness which is from God by faith: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "that I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, becoming conformed unto his death; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "if by any means I may attain unto the resurrection from the dead. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Not that I have already obtained, or am already made perfect: but I press on, if so be that I may lay hold on that for which also I was laid hold on by Christ Jesus. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Brethren, I count not myself yet to have laid hold: but one thing ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", forgetting the things which are behind, and stretching forward to the things which are before, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I press on toward the goal unto the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let us therefore, as many as are perfect, be thus minded: and if in anything ye are otherwise minded, this also shall God reveal unto you: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "only, whereunto we have attained, by that same ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " let us walk.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Brethren, be ye imitators together of me, and mark them that so walk even as ye have us for an ensample. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For many walk, of whom I told you often, and now tell you even weeping, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " the enemies of the cross of Christ: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "whose end is perdition, whose god is the belly, and ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " glory is in their shame, who mind earthly things. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For our citizenship is in heaven; whence also we wait for a Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "PHP 3:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "who shall fashion anew the body of our humiliation, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " conformed to the body of his glory, according to the working whereby he is able even to subject all things unto himself.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "PHP.3.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "PHP.3.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "PHP.4",
    "number": "4",
    "bookId": "PHP"
  },
  "previous": {
    "id": "PHP.2",
